# Before: SetBuilder lowered with a binder SymbolId, but no Lean constructor
# protected that identity from capture.
# Now: the target predicate uses a SymbolId-derived local binder.
have S set = {x R: x = x}
S = S
# Boundary: changing the binder identity changes the retained value/check and
# is rejected; the local x never enters the outer context.
# Evidence: focused Rust and ignored real-Mathlib gates are recorded in the ledger.
